{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"neidhardtIII","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","text":"WellTemperament","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Three fifths — C→G, G→D, D→A — are each narrowed by ⅙ of the Pythagorean comma"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(≈ 698.045 cents). Six fifths — A→E, B→F♯, F♯→C♯, C♯→A♭, E♭→B♭, B♭→F — are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each narrowed by 1\/12 of the Pythagorean comma (≈ 700.000 cents). The remaining"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"three fifths — E→B, A♭→E♭, F→C — are pure. The circle closes exactly:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"3×(1\/6) + 6×(1\/12) = 1 Pythagorean comma."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"From "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Sectio Canonis Harmonici","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" (Königsberg, 1724). Differs from "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem\/neidhardtII","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only in the placement of the sixth-comma group on the flat side: E♭→B♭ is tempered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"here where it is pure in Neidhardt II, and F→C is pure here where it is tempered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in Neidhardt II."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:10IvorTuning0B6SystemPA2A15WellTemperamentVRszrlE12neidhardtIIIAEvpZ","title":"neidhardtIII","modules":[{"name":"IvorTuning"}],"roleHeading":"Type Property","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Self","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"WellTemperament","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}]},"symbolKind":"property","extendedModule":"IvorTuning","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"neidhardtIII","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WellTemperament","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivortuning\/tuningsystem\/neidhardtiii"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem\/neidhardtIII","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"Neidhardt III (“Large City”; Johann Georg Neidhardt, 1724).","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","title":"IvorTuning","url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning","abstract":[{"text":"Musical pitch, interval, and tuning system types.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/WellTemperament":{"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"WellTemperament","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A tuning system in which all twelve keys are usable but have distinct tonal characters,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"achieved by distributing the Pythagorean comma unevenly around the circle of fifths."}],"role":"symbol","title":"WellTemperament","url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WellTemperament","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/TuningSystem/neidhardtIII":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem\/neidhardtIII","title":"neidhardtIII","role":"symbol","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WellTemperament"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}]},"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"neidhardtIII","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WellTemperament","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning\/tuningsystem\/neidhardtiii","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Neidhardt III (“Large City”; Johann Georg Neidhardt, 1724)."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/TuningSystem":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem","title":"TuningSystem","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TuningSystem","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TuningSystem","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning\/tuningsystem","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that describes a musical tuning system."}]},"doc://IvorTuning/docu